=== Text #6 ===
> PLEASE READ[ CARE]FULLY BEFORE PROCEEDING WITH YOUR[ APPLIC]ATION.
We are a language centre created in 1984 and located in Brussels, Belgium.
We are experts in language teaching in Belgium and abroad.
We have several departments and centres and teach a variety of[ customers] ([individual]s, companies, international institutions in Brussels and Luxembourg).
We have a teaching team which is[ composed] of over[ 600] freelance teachers who teach more than 25 languages.
We are looking for teachers to teach by[ vide]oconference, using our own virtual classroom platform (including a virtual white[board]).
We offer 30-minute classes to learners from different profiles ([individual]s or companies, mostly located in Europe).
We offer the opportunity to teach from home or remotely with flexibility to choose the hours you want. Our platform is available 24/[7], 365 days a year.
We provide teaching material in Dutch, English, French, German, Italian, Portuguese, Russian and Spanish.
We offer ongoing training to our teachers to help them develop their teaching skills online.
- suitable IT equipment (computer, webcam, headset and a broadband internet connection).
Skype ID: Skype will be used for a potential interview.
Please record a short introduction.* This field is required Tell us who you are and why you'd like to become part of our team.
We'd just like to ask you a few questions about your teaching philosophy. This allows us to understand your approach to the classroom and how you would teach online.
What days/hours ([GMT]+2) would you be available to teach? Note that entering availabilities does not yet constitute a valid job offer.

